Sval: give pages the bundled emoji font under Strict

A new RFPTarget, EmojiFontBundled, makes emoji fallback resolve to the
bundled Twemoji Mozilla instead of font.name-list.emoji, so emoji render the
same whatever the OS and its emoji font version. It is a strict control.
gfxPlatformFontList keeps the bundled list beside the pref one, chosen per
FontVisibilityProvider, so the target is Doc-gated and granularOverrides
lifts it per site. The emoji pref is global and also styles the browser's
own UI, so a pref cannot do this.

Upstream ships TwemojiMozilla.ttf only on Windows and Linux; browser/fonts
and the package manifest ship it on macOS too, where Sval's mozconfig turns
on --enable-bundled-fonts so CoreTextFontList activates it.

diff --git a/browser/fonts/moz.build b/browser/fonts/moz.build
index 0ebf2de60f..49e3b29a2c 100644
--- a/browser/fonts/moz.build
+++ b/browser/fonts/moz.build
@@ -2,6 +2,6 @@
 # License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
-if CONFIG["MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT"] in ("windows", "gtk"):
+if CONFIG["MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT"] in ("windows", "gtk", "cocoa"):
     DIST_SUBDIR = ""
     FINAL_TARGET_FILES.fonts += ["TwemojiMozilla.ttf"]
diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
index 554f0c2eab..1a4fc28204 100644
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
